  "_meta": {
    "scenario": "getDecisionSync §4a intent-law vectors + blank-message fallback envelope",
    "semantics": "§4a intent law (re-recorded 2026-11-13; every pre-§4a pin below is a documented legacy-defect change, not silent drift): an artifact WORD is not an artifact REQUEST. Quoted/code spans are masked first; clauses split on [.!?\\n;]+ AFTER alnum-dot-alnum runs ('file.docx', 'v2.5') become spaces (filename/version/decimal dots are not clause boundaries — 'create file.docx' binds docs); an artifact word counts as requested only when a production cue precedes it in the same clause — all cue/artifact/direction/negation/meta relations compare MATCH STARTS by order only, never end-vs-start (adjacent matches share their boundary character, so end-vs-start is off-by-one there; fixed in both engines 2026-11-13; this is why 'export as xlsx'/'generate pdf report' were misses before) (cue vocabulary is ENGLISH-ONLY — a non-Latin verb with a Latin artifact word falls gracefully to standard_chat); negation before the word vetoes it; convert/export governs the word directly as the SOURCE format (the word after a to/into/as direction word is the output); summary/outline-style meta phrases mark discussed material; two+ requested intents are ambiguous ('in-process-deliverable-ambiguous') — INTENT_ORDER precedence retired. Unicode \\p{L}/\\p{N}/\\p{M} consuming word classes in BOTH engines: caféexcel/résumébuilder no longer split, bare résumé matches its own word, résumé2 honestly misses. Honest confidence: 0.8 verb-bound, 0.5 miss/ambiguous — the retired blanket 1.0 was false certainty. Anatomy/3d/cad vocabulary stays standard_chat (retired 2026-11-06/07) unless a §4a cue-bound request survives ('make an exploded diagram in html' -> html_render; 'interior design with html' -> html_render because 'design' is a production cue now). F02 (re-recorded 2026-11-16, typed-relation law): a request is a request whatever its politeness - 'would like'/\"'d like\" are production cues, so 'I would like a spreadsheet of the figures' routes excel; a COGNITIVE or REPORT frame around the format word is never a request - 'I would like to understand how a pdf stores fonts', 'walk me through how to generate a docx', 'she exported a pptx last Friday', 'it looked like a pdf' and 'Explain what a PDF and a DOCX are' all stay standard_chat. Polysemy stays polysemy ('deck' of cards / terrace deck / poker deck). Honest decided_by vocabulary: -none (no deliverable found, never reported as a match), -match (exactly one), -multiple (two or more requested deliverables, recorded in task_constraints as 'deliverable-request=<mode>' in first-appearance order; active_mode stays standard_chat because the scan must not invent a winner and the injection layer arms every requested contract). The retired -ambiguous label conflated 'several deliverables' with 'uncertain', which silently lost one requested output. F02b (re-recorded 2026-11-16, generalisation law): the didactic frame now also covers step NOUN PHRASES ('the steps for making', 'procedure for'), which frame the whole clause exactly the way 'how to' does; using/on/of/for mark MATERIAL or TOPIC and never a second deliverable (the container particles in/as/into/to stay out of that set on purpose); a transform cue is the verb PLUS its particle even when the material sits between them ('turn this PDF into a DOCX'), and a bare transform verb with a production cue in the gap is an unfinished transform, never a source role for the later ask; a HYPOTHETICAL FRAME (a conditional antecedent whose own production cue governs the format word, plus a turn-level didactic/interrogative frame) discusses production instead of requesting a file, while an affirmative conditional without such a frame keeps its deliverable. One pin moved with the law: 'put these numbers into my spreadsheet' now names the spreadsheet as the DESTINATION (excel) instead of being a cue-less miss.",
    "comparison": "semantic",
    "notes": "Field-for-field (mode/skill/decided_by/trim/confidence) — regex existence only, no span capture. Re-recorded 2026-11-13 for the §4a intent law (brief §4): the OLD corpus pinned the ASCII-\\b quirks, INTENT_ORDER precedence and confidence 1 as contracts; brief §6 reclassifies those as legacy defects, so their pins moved to the OPPOSITE behavior. F02 2026-11-16 re-record adds the polite-desire cues, the cognitive/report frame law and the explicit multi-deliverable record; the decided_by pin vocabulary changed from -ambiguous to -multiple, and a plain miss now records -none instead of claiming -match. Every changed pin is the intended new law, verified against the live oracle. F02b 2026-11-16 (brief section 4 generalisation): 12 new vectors for the action-vs-discussion, material-vs-subject, discontinuous-transform-particle and hypothetical-frame axes, plus the single documented pin change above. The frozen ANSWER KEY for those prompts lives in __tests__/decision/generalization-f02b.test.ts (written before the repair and first run as a reproduction); this corpus only pins that both engines reach the same outcome.",
    "harness": "__tests__/rust-golden/decision-parity.test.ts",
